To implement the Round-Robin simulation, we first validate the input parameters to ensure they meet the specified constraints. We then initialize the current time `t` to 0 and prepare the ready queue. Processes with an arrival time of 0 are added to the ready queue initially. The simulation proceeds by repeatedly selecting the next process to execute, running it for up to the quantum time, and managing context switches and new arrivals. Processes are tracked until all have completed, and their completion times, turnaround times, and waiting times are recorded.

