The problem requires finding the maximum weight independent set on a path graph with specific tie-breaking rules. The solution uses dynamic programming to track the best possible states, considering both inclusion and exclusion of each node. After computing the DP, the optimal set is reconstructed based on the stored states, ensuring the tie-breaking criteria are met.

